Track 3: Tape-Hiss Siphon at 0400 Hours
- Story & Context: The legendary finale of the scene’s emergence occurred when an unnamed harbor dispatcher spliced a recorded black metal tremolo guitar riff into the harbor’s automated automated fog-warning broadcast system. As two massive container ships maneuvered blindly through a pitch-black, zero-visibility dawn, their automated sensors bounced the low-fidelity guitar loop back and forth across the bay like a monstrous, cozy call-and-response refrain. By sunrise, the entire bay was humming with a giant, warm, tape-saturated resonance that cleared the psychological dread of the fog for everyone on shore. A local radio operator preserved the event on reel-to-reel, capturing the quiet radio chatter that capped the myth: "Did you hear the iron monster call for breakfast?"
